# harmgrow — is the morphology bound harmonic?
# x=ln r, sum x = 0; pitch w=1/r; pair cost = comb dissonance
# of log2(r_j/r_i); drive -g_i x_i. NO maximum size in U.

== 1. the rung set (what 'consonant' means here) ==
comb_limit=0  nrungs=   1  u span=[-0.00,+0.00] => ratio span up to 1x
comb_limit=2  nrungs=   7  u span=[-2.00,+2.00] => ratio span up to 4x
comb_limit=4  nrungs=  41  u span=[-4.00,+4.00] => ratio span up to 16x
comb_limit=6  nrungs= 211  u span=[-6.00,+6.00] => ratio span up to 64x

NOTE: the comb has a FINITE SPAN. Past the outermost rung the
cost grows quadratically with no rung left to relax to. That is
the only thing here that could bound a size, and it is made of
intervals (dimensionless), not of lengths.

