== 4. HOW SHARP IS THE QUANTISATION? vs lock width sigma ==
sweep g0 = 4..80 at each sigma; count distinct rungs visited and
how much of the sweep is spent locked (|u-u_k| < sigma/10).
 sigma  rungs_visited  jumps  frac_locked  max_ratio
  0.02              6      5        1.000       6.00
  0.05              6      5        1.000       6.00
  0.10              6      5        1.000       6.00
  0.15              6      5        1.000       6.01
  0.20              6      5        1.000       6.01
  0.30              6      5        1.000       6.03
  0.50              6     60        1.000       6.09

reading: a stiff comb (small sigma) locks hard but reaches few
rungs; a loose comb reaches many but holds none. Quantisation
needs a window in sigma, not a limit.

== 4b. WHEN DOES QUANTISATION EXIST? comb vs the cell's own
energetic preference. Comb curvature at sigma=0.05 is 400.
     kE  rungs_visited  jumps/151  max_log2_achieved (pref 3.000)
      1              6          5  2.585
     10              9          8  3.000
     50             13         12  3.000
    200             22        150  3.000
    400             28        150  3.000
   2000             40        150  3.000
   8000             42        150  3.000

reading: few rungs + few jumps = long plateaux = QUANTISED.
jumps ~ every sample = the elastic term wins and size follows
preference continuously. Quantisation is a WINDOW in kE, and
max_log2 < 3.000 means the comb held the cell BELOW the size
its own energy wanted — a bound, made of intervals.

