== 7. THE BOUND — push one cell arbitrarily hard ==
   g0      r0/r_nb    log2     rung    max|grad|
   0.5       1.000   +0.000    1/1     6.3e-07
   1.0       2.000   +1.000    2/1     1.3e-13
   2.0       3.000   +1.585    3/1     1.4e-06
   3.0       6.001   +2.585    6/1     1.4e-06
   4.0      12.002   +3.585   12/1     1.3e-06
   5.0      23.004   +4.524   23/1     1.5e-06
   6.0      47.008   +5.555   47/1     1.4e-06
   7.0      64.024   +6.001   64/1     9.1e-07
   8.0      64.049   +6.001   64/1     1.1e-06
  10.0      64.098   +6.002   64/1     1.6e-06

reading: the outermost rung is 64/1 at u=6. Past it the wall is
quadratic and the drive is linear, so equilibrium sits at
u = u_max + g*sigma^2*ln2/2 — finite for any g, but UNBOUNDED as
g grows. The comb QUANTISES size; it does not CAP it.
